    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n11 Wingfield is an immaculately presented and attractive brick fronted 4-bedroom semi-detached house which offers pristine, light-filled and well-proportioned accommodation with the bonus of an attic conversion; a B1 energy rating, solar panels, a landscaped rear garden; off-street parking with EV charger; and an excellent location within a small development in a mature and popular residential enclave of Bray that overlooks an attractive amenity green\n\nThis home really has everything to offer any discerning buyer so early viewing comes highly recommended. \n\nBuilt in 2014 by Brian M Durkan, Wingfield is a small development which consists of 17 houses. Finished to a high standard and specification throughout, the spacious and elegantly presented accommodation extends to 116sq.m + an additional 30sq.m with the attic conversion. There is private \noff-street parking for 2 vehicles with an EV charger, to the front of the house on a cobble lock driveway. \n\nOn entering the house one is immediately welcomed by an impressive entrance hallway with a guest WC; to the left is a spacious and well appointed living room with wall panelling; the rear of the house is home to a lovely open plan kitchen and dining room with double doors leading seamlessly into the garden; there is also a useful utility room with a door \nleading out to the side passageway. Rising upstairs to the 1st floor there are 4 bedrooms (the main bedroom is ensuite); a hot press and an elegantly presented family bathroom. The attic conversion is a fantastic addition to the house comprising of a large attic room and an ensuite shower room. \n\nWingfield is nestled on the northern end of Bray and within close proximity to a superb choice of local services and amenities including a communal park with direct access from the development; primary and secondary schools; supermarkets; sports and recreational facilities such as Bray Emmets GAA, \nWoodbrook Golf Club, Bray Harbour and seafront promenade, a plethora of shops and businesses on Bray Main Street; cafes, bars and restaurants. \n\nBray is a large and popular coastal town situated approximately 22km south of Dublin City Centre. The area has excellent transport links with regular DART services from either Bray or the newly opened Woodbrook Station; several Dublin Bus routes passing by the entrance to the estate, the Luas is close by in Cherrywood and Carrickmines, and the N11/M11/M50 road network provides easy access to Dublin and beyond."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall: - \nA welcoming entrance with laminate wood flooring and decorative radiator cover.\n\nGuest W.C: - \nLarge suite with wood panelling, tiled floor, part tiled walls, W.C. and wash hand basin.\n\nLiving Room: - \nA bright room with views over the private front garden. Features include wood panelling, laminate wood flooring, marble fireplace with granite hearth and Wander's inset stove. Double doors lead through to…\n\nKitchen/Dining: - \nStretching across the rear of the property with polished porcelain tiled floor. The large dining area has room for a family sized table and double doors to the rear garden. The kitchen is fitted with a Nolan's design high gloss kitchen topped with black granite and features a large breakfast bar. The integrated appliances include a 5-burner gas hob, Zanussi double oven, dishwasher, fridge/freezer and Electrolux microwave.\n\nUtility Room: - \nWith fitted storage, counter space, tiled floor and door to side passage. There are provisions for a washing machine and a tumble dryer.\n\nLanding: - \nWith access to the shelved hot press.\n\nBedroom 1: - \nA well proportioned double room with picture window overlooking the amenity green to the front of the house and double fitted wardrobes.\n\nEnsuite: - \nPart tiled walls, tiled floor, W.C., wall mounted sink and double length shower.\n\nBedroom 2: - \nA good size double room with fitted wardrobes to the rear of the property.\n\nBedroom 3: - \nA generous double room with fitted wardrobes overlooking the rear garden.\n\nBathroom: - \nA family bathroom incorporating a tiled floor, part tiled walls, bath with shower, W.C. and wall mounted sink.\n\nBedroom 4: - \nA single room with wood flooring to the front of the property currently used as a home office.\n\nAttic Room: - \nAn extensive double room with 2 Velux roof lights, access to eaves storage and plush carpeting.\n\nEnsuite: - \nA fully tiled suite with corner shower with sliding doors and shampoo shelf, pedestal sink and W.C.\n\nGARDEN - \n\n\nFront: - \nA walled front garden with cobble locked drive surrounded by mature hedging and well stocked colourful planting beds. A gated side access through to…\n\nRear: - \nA silver granite patio leads out to an Astro-lawn with putting green. The raised planting beds surround the garden that burst with colour and foliage at all times of the year. There is hedging to the rear and a garden shed.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Features:</li><li> Immaculately and beautifully presented 4-bedroom semi-detached house with a converted attic.</li><li> Spacious, light-filled and well-appointed accommodation extending to 116sqm + 30sqm (attic).</li><li> Landscaped rear garden with a paved patio and a putting green.</li><li> Small residential development of only 17 houses overlooking an amenity green.</li><li> Excellent location with close proximity to all local services and amenities.</li><li> Choice of local primary & secondary schools; transport links including bus, rail and road.</li><li> Private off-street parking for two vehicles.</li><li> Built 2014 by Brian M Durkan.</li><li> Solar panels and an EV charger.</li><li> BER B1</li><li></li><li>Services:</li><li> GFCH (gas fired central heating)</li><li> Mains water and sewerage.</li><li> Usual TV, phone and broadband services are available.</ul>"
      },
